          "content": {
            "size": 100251,
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"data\":{\"jobs\":[{\"id\":\"7768a357-7d39-4883-bf8e-91685752cde6\",\"source_id\":\"2411865207\",\"obfuscated_id\":41977882,\"title\":\"Software Tools Developer\",\"organization\":\"Ford Motor Company\",\"job_url\":\"https://efds.fa.em5.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/BlueOvalCity/job/72422\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-13T19:17:20.656585Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Dearborn, MI, US\",\"Dearborn, MI, USA\",\"Dearborn, MI, United States\",\"Dearborn, Michigan, US\",\"Dearborn, Michigan, USA\",\"Dearborn, Michigan, United States\",\"MI, US\",\"MI, USA\",\"MI, United States\",\"Michigan, US\",\"Michigan, USA\",\"Michigan, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"207a4c9e-e30e-49b4-8340-5fb1a9d55bd8\",\"company_image_id\":\"xfljw80gbvj7wfsbrd3s\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":85400,\"salary_max_value\":160000,\"salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":85400,\"ai_salary_max_value\":160000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Python\",\"Test automation\",\"Software development\",\"CI/CD pipelines\",\"Linux\",\"QNX\",\"Android\",\"POSIX\",\"Windows\",\"Automotive ECU testing\",\"CAN\",\"DoCAN\",\"DoIP\",\"AUTOSAR\",\"Data analytics\",\"Visualization\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Product Creation and Industrialization (PC\\u0026I) brings together Ford’s vehicle,\\nelectric, digital and design teams with our global manufacturing system. Working\\nas one end-to-end organization, we turn ideas into high-quality vehicles,\\nsoftware and experiences across gas, hybrid and electric, designed around what\\ncustomers need.\\n\\n \\n\\nIn this position... \\n\\nThe successful candidate will be part of the Test Automation Tools (TAT)\\ndevelopment team involved in the delivery of SW solutions that facilitate\\nautomated testing of the latest automotive, infotainment and connectivity\\ntechnologies. You will work alongside the automation architect, design \\u0026\\nimplement some of the foundational software components and tools used in\\nautomation. You will also provide guidance to team members on proper usage of\\nautomation test libraries and test script development.\\n\\n\\nRESPONSIBILITIES\\n\\nWhat you'll do...\\n\\n * Taking a role in the development of advanced automated testing solutions. \\n   This includes testing framework and tools, and test libraries that interface\\n   with vehicle electronic control units (ECUs) which are consumed by internal\\n   and external teams.\\n\\n * Analyze and decompose complex software systems and collaborate with\\n   cross-functional teams to influence design for testability.\\n\\n * Drive adoption of best practices in code health, testing, and maintainability\\n\\n * Actively participate in code reviews and provide coaching to fellow team\\n   members on automation practice.\\n\\n\\nQUALIFICATIONS\\n\\nYou'll have...\\n\\n * Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field. \\n\\n * 5+ year experience in software development.\\n\\n * 2+ year experience in automation and tool development.\\n\\n * 2+ year experience in Python development.\\n\\n * 1+ year Experience building, integrating, and deploying software within\\n   large-scale, complex systems.\\n\\n * Self-driven with mentorship qualities to foster growth of both internal and\\n   external team members.\\n\\n \\n\\nEven better, you may have...\\n\\n * Experience using Python in large scale projects or code bases.\\n\\n * Experience building and configuring Continuous Integration/Continuous\\n   Delivery (CI/CD) pipelines.\\n\\n * Strong knowledge of operating system architecture (Linux, QNX, Android, POSIX\\n   and Windows).\\n\\n * Experience with automotive ECU testing and strong understanding in CAN.\\n\\n * Experience in DoCAN, DoIP, AUTOSAR.\\n\\n * Exposure to Intrepid and Vector products.\\n\\n * Experience with data analytics and visualization.\\n\\n * Analytical with the ability to produce creative and effective software\\n   solutions to problems.\\n\\n * Strong communication and interpersonal skills.\\n\\n \\n\\nYou may not check every box, or your experience may look a little different from\\nwhat we've outlined, but if you think you can bring value to Ford Motor Company,\\nwe encourage you to apply!\\n\\n \\n\\nAs an established global company, we offer the benefit of choice. You can choose\\nwhat your Ford future will look like: will your story span the globe, or keep\\nyou close to home? Will your career be a deep dive into what you love, or a\\nseries of new teams and new skills? Will you be a leader, a changemaker, a\\ntechnical expert, a culture builder…or all of the above? No matter what you\\nchoose, we offer a work life that works for you, including:\\n\\n• Immediate medical, dental, vision and prescription drug coverage\\n\\n• Flexible family care days, paid parental leave, new parent ramp-up programs,\\nsubsidized back-up child care and more\\n\\n• Family building benefits including adoption and surrogacy expense\\nreimbursement, fertility treatments, and more\\n\\n• Vehicle discount program for employees and family members and management\\nleases\\n\\n• Tuition assistance\\n\\n• Established and active employee resource groups\\n\\n• Paid time off for individual and team community service \\n\\n• A generous schedule of paid holidays, including the week between Christmas and\\nNew Year’s Day \\n\\n• Paid time off and the option to purchase additional vacation time. \\n\\n \\n\\nThis position is a range of salary grades 6 -8 and ranges from\\n$85,400-$160,000.     \\n\\nFinal determination of salary grade will be based on candidate's skills and\\nexperience, and base salary will be set within the applicable range according to\\njob scope, responsibility and competitive market value.\\n\\n \\n\\nFor more information on salary and benefits, click here:\\nhttps://fordcareers.co/GSR [https://fordcareers.co/GSR]\\n\\n \\n\\nVisa sponsorship is not available for this position.\\n\\n \\n\\nCandidates for positions with Ford Motor Company must be legally authorized to\\nwork in the United States. Verification of employment eligibility will be\\nrequired at the time of hire.\\n\\n \\n\\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive\\nconsideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, age, sex,\\nnational origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability status or\\nprotected veteran status. In the United States, if you need a reasonable\\naccommodation for the online application process due to a disability, please\\ncall 1-888-336-0660.\\n\\n \\n\\nThis position is hybrid with a requirement to be onsite four or more days per\\nweek. \\n\\n#LI-Hybrid    #LI-MG3\"},{\"id\":\"464067ad-5edf-42bd-b650-6163105c563d\",\"source_id\":\"2412728666\",\"obfuscated_id\":42039022,\"title\":\"Software Tools Developer\",\"organization\":\"Ford\",\"job_url\":\"https://jobs.ford.com/careers/job/563568453995885-software-tools-developer-dearborn-mi-united-states\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-14T03:15:54.867577Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Dearborn, MI, US\",\"Dearborn, MI, USA\",\"Dearborn, MI, United States\",\"Dearborn, Michigan, US\",\"Dearborn, Michigan, USA\",\"Dearborn, Michigan, United States\",\"MI, US\",\"MI, USA\",\"MI, United States\",\"Michigan, US\",\"Michigan, USA\",\"Michigan, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"efcdff9f-6e7c-4e39-8fe2-b39466f3273c\",\"company_image_id\":\"ahnr8misgpz6ts2rp0nc\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":85400,\"salary_max_value\":160000,\"salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":85400,\"ai_salary_max_value\":160000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Python\",\"Test automation\",\"Software development\",\"CI/CD\",\"Linux\",\"QNX\",\"Android\",\"POSIX\",\"Windows\",\"CAN\",\"DoCAN\",\"DoIP\",\"AUTOSAR\",\"Data analytics\",\"Data visualization\",\"Code review\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Product Creation and Industrialization (PC\\u0026I) brings together Ford’s vehicle, electric, digital and design teams with our global manufacturing system. Working as one end-to-end organization, we turn ideas into high-quality vehicles, software and experiences across gas, hybrid and electric, designed around what customers need.\\nIn this position... \\nThe successful candidate will be part of the Test Automation Tools (TAT) development team involved in the delivery of SW solutions that facilitate automated testing of the latest automotive, infotainment and connectivity technologies. You will work alongside the automation architect, design \\u0026 implement some of the foundational software components and tools used in automation. You will also provide guidance to team members on proper usage of automation test libraries and test script development.\\nWhat you'll do...\\nTaking a role in the development of advanced automated testing solutions. This includes testing framework and tools, and test libraries that interface with vehicle electronic control units (ECUs) which are consumed by internal and external teams.\\nAnalyze and decompose complex software systems and collaborate with cross-functional teams to influence design for testability.\\nDrive adoption of best practices in code health, testing, and maintainability\\nActively participate in code reviews and provide coaching to fellow team members on automation practice.\\nYou'll have...\\nBachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field. \\n5+ year experience in software development.\\n2+ year experience in automation and tool development.\\n2+ year experience in Python development.\\n1+ year Experience building, integrating, and deploying software within large-scale, complex systems.\\nSelf-driven with mentorship qualities to foster growth of both internal and external team members.\\nEven better, you may have...\\nExperience using Python in large scale projects or code bases.\\nExperience building and configuring Continuous Integration/Continuous Delivery (CI/CD) pipelines.\\nStrong knowledge of operating system architecture (Linux, QNX, Android, POSIX and Windows).\\nExperience with automotive ECU testing and strong understanding in CAN.\\nExperience in DoCAN, DoIP, AUTOSAR.\\nExposure to Intrepid and Vector products.\\nExperience with data analytics and visualization.\\nAnalytical with the ability to produce creative and effective software solutions to problems.\\nStrong communication and interpersonal skills.\\nYou may not check every box, or your experience may look a little different from what we've outlined, but if you think you can bring value to Ford Motor Company, we encourage you to apply!\\nAs an established global company, we offer the benefit of choice. You can choose what your Ford future will look like: will your story span the globe, or keep you close to home? Will your career be a deep dive into what you love, or a series of new teams and new skills? Will you be a leader, a changemaker, a technical expert, a culture builder…or all of the above? No matter what you choose, we offer a work life that works for you, including:\\n• Immediate medical, dental, vision and prescription drug coverage\\n• Flexible family care days, paid parental leave, new parent ramp-up programs, subsidized back-up child care and more\\n• Family building benefits including adoption and surrogacy expense reimbursement, fertility treatments, and more\\n• Vehicle discount program for employees and family members and management leases\\n• Tuition assistance\\n• Established and active employee resource groups\\n• Paid time off for individual and team community service \\n• A generous schedule of paid holidays, including the week between Christmas and New Year’s Day \\n• Paid time off and the option to purchase additional vacation time. \\nThis position is a range of salary grades 6 -8 and ranges from $85,400-$160,000. \\nFinal determination of salary grade will be based on candidate's skills and experience, and base salary will be set within the applicable range according to job scope, responsibility and competitive market value.\\nFor more information on salary and benefits, click here: https://fordcareers.co/GSR\\nVisa sponsorship is not available for this position.\\nCandidates for positions with Ford Motor Company must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Verification of employment eligibility will be required at the time of hire.\\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, age, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability status or protected veteran status. In the United States, if you need a reasonable accommodation for the online application process due to a disability, please call 1-888-336-0660.\\nThis position is hybrid with a requirement to be onsite four or more days per week. \\n#LI-Hybrid #LI-MG3\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Product Creation and Industrialization (PC\\u0026I) brings together Ford’s vehicle, electric, digital and design teams with our global manufacturing system.\",\"Working as one end-to-end organization, we turn ideas into high-quality vehicles, software and experiences across gas, hybrid and electric, designed around what customers need.\",\"As an established global company, we offer the benefit of choice. You can choose what your Ford future will look like: will your story span the globe, or keep you close to home? Will your career be a deep dive into what you love, or a series of new teams and new skills? Will you be a leader, a changemaker, a technical expert, a culture builder…or all of the above?\",\"No matter what you choose, we offer a work life that works for you.\"],\"about_role\":\"The Test Automation Tools (TAT) development team delivers SW solutions that facilitate automated testing of automotive, infotainment, and connectivity technologies. You will work alongside the automation architect to design and implement foundational software components and tools used in automation, and provide guidance on automation test libraries and test script development.\",\"annual_salary\":[\"$85,400-$160,000\"],\"benefits\":[\"Immediate medical, dental, vision and prescription drug coverage\",\"Flexible family care days, paid parental leave, new parent ramp-up programs, subsidized back-up child care and more\",\"Family building benefits including adoption and surrogacy expense reimbursement, fertility treatments, and more\",\"Vehicle discount program for employees and family members and management leases\",\"Tuition assistance\",\"Established and active employee resource groups\",\"Paid time off for individual and team community service\",\"A generous schedule of paid holidays, including the week between Christmas and New Year’s Day\",\"Paid time off and the option to purchase additional vacation time\"],\"education_level\":[\"Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field\"],\"equal_opportunity\":[\"We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, age, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability status or protected veteran status.\",\"In the United States, if you need a reasonable accommodation for the online application process due to a disability, please call 1-888-336-0660.\"],\"experience_level\":[\"5+ years of experience in software development\",\"2+ years of experience in automation and tool development\",\"2+ years of experience in Python development\",\"1+ year of experience building, integrating, and deploying software within large-scale, complex systems\"],\"location\":[\"Hybrid\"],\"requirements\":[\"Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.\",\"5+ years of experience in software development.\",\"2+ years of experience in automation and tool development.\",\"2+ years of experience in Python development.\",\"1+ year of experience building, integrating, and deploying software within large-scale, complex systems.\",\"Self-driven with mentorship qualities to foster growth of both internal and external team members.\",\"Experience using Python in large scale projects or code bases.\",\"Experience building and configuring Continuous Integration/Continuous Delivery (CI/CD) pipelines.\",\"Strong knowledge of operating system architecture (Linux, QNX, Android, POSIX and Windows).\",\"Experience with automotive ECU testing and strong understanding in CAN.\",\"Experience in DoCAN, DoIP, AUTOSAR.\",\"Exposure to Intrepid and Vector products.\",\"Experience with data analytics and visualization.\",\"Analytical with the ability to produce creative and effective software solutions to problems.\",\"Strong communication and interpersonal skills.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Take a role in the development of advanced automated testing solutions, including testing frameworks, tools, and test libraries that interface with vehicle ECUs.\",\"Analyze and decompose complex software systems and collaborate with cross-functional teams to influence design for testability.\",\"Drive adoption of best practices in code health, testing, and maintainability.\",\"Actively participate in code reviews and provide coaching to fellow team members on automation practice.\"],\"skills\":[\"Python\",\"Automation\",\"Tool Development\",\"Software Development\",\"CI/CD\",\"Operating System Architecture\",\"Automotive ECU Testing\",\"CAN\",\"DoCAN\",\"DoIP\",\"AUTOSAR\",\"Data Analytics\",\"Data Visualization\"],\"work_type\":[\"Hybrid\",\"Onsite (four or more days per week)\"]}},{\"id\":\"6dfbd0ba-5c75-4dbd-9b50-6a740777c02d\",\"source_id\":\"2396089905\",\"obfuscated_id\":40955392,\"title\":\"Applications\",\"organization\":\"iA Financial Group (Industrial Alliance)\",\"job_url\":\"https://ia.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Professional_US/job/Grand-Rapids-Michigan/Applications_JR10027453-1\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-03T10:18:05.621653Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Grand Rapids, MI, US\",\"Grand Rapids, MI, USA\",\"Grand Rapids, MI, United States\",\"Grand Rapids, Michigan, US\",\"Grand Rapids, Michigan, USA\",\"Grand Rapids, Michigan, United States\",\"MI, US\",\"MI, USA\",\"MI, United States\",\"Michigan, US\",\"Michigan, USA\",\"Michigan, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"78b98845-3e7c-4b1a-fca6-6f065789d9d6\",\"company_image_id\":\"v1499434540/unnhsby74i3x0bqkbcan.jpg\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":75000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":110000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Vehicle washing\",\"Surface preparation\",\"Attention to detail\",\"Quality control\",\"Customer service\",\"Time management\",\"Process adherence\",\"Manual dexterity\",\"Safety compliance\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Job Description\\nWash Bay Technician\\nBuild the future with us\\nAre you driven by [industry or company mission] and eager to contribute to a company that helps its clients feel confident and secure about their future? As a Wash Bay Technician, you will play a key role in preparing vehicles for protective coatings and other shop services, ensuring high‑quality results and excellent customer service.\\nThis position is a great opportunity to showcase your skills and fully realize your potential within a caring and trustworthy company. Here, people and their development are at the heart of our priorities, fostering an environment that encourages collaboration and innovation.\\nWhat you’ll accomplish with us\\nAs a Wash Bay Technician, you’ll be at the core of our mission. Here are the main responsibilities:\\nPrepare and wash vehicles for protective coating and related services\\nPay close attention to debris such as road tar and environmental particles\\nPerform washing, claying, and surface preparation with precision\\nFollow instructions, procedures, and processes to maintain service quality\\nProvide great customer service while supporting overall shop operations\\nWhat could accelerate your success in this role\\nWe’re looking for someone who:\\nIs known for their ability to learn new tasks and processes quickly and accurately\\nStands out for their attention to detail and commitment to quality\\nDemonstrates strong work ethic in fast‑paced environments\\nIs recognized for their ability to follow procedures and maintain consistency\\nHas basic knowledge of vehicle washing and surface preparation\\nWork Environment\\nThis position works in a shop setting with some outdoor exposure during the workday. The employee will work with:\\nPower washer hoses and spray guns\\nWet indoor areas with scrub pads, chemical lines, and spray bottles\\nPhysical Demands\\nTo successfully perform this job, the employee must be able to:\\nUse hands to handle tools, reach, and communicate\\nStand, walk, stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl frequently\\nOccasionally sit, climb, or balance\\nRegularly lift/move up to 10 lbs., and occasionally up to 50 lbs.\\nMaintain strong visual abilities (close, distance, color, peripheral, depth perception, focus)\\nStand and/or move most of the day with minimal sitting\\nSupervisory Responsibility\\nThis position has no supervisory responsibilities.\\nWhy you’ll love working with us\\nA work environment where learning and development merge with a collective pursuit of excellence\\nA healthy, safe, fair, and inclusive environment where potential can be freely expressed and developed\\nThe opportunity to work in a supportive, collaborative shop environment\\nCompetitive benefits: Flexible Health, Dental and Vision insurance, 401(k) + company match, PTO Plan, employee and family assistance program, ergonomic furniture program, performance bonus, and more\\nStatement\\nThis job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the employee. It is not a contract and should not be construed as a guarantee of employment for any specific period of time. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Great Lakes Companies and all its divisions are an Equal Opportunity Employer.\\nApply now and get ahead of your career, where your talent really belongs!\\nStill unsure about applying? At iA, we believe in potential and value diverse experiences. If this role inspires you, go ahead and apply — your place might be with us, and we want to get to know you.\\nApplicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We are unable to support or take over sponsorship of employment visas at this time, including H-1B visas and participation in STEM OPT work authorizations.\\nCompany\\niA American Warranty, L.P.\\nPosting End Date\\n2026-10-26\\n\\nAbout us\\niA American Warranty LP, American Amicable Group of Companies, iA American Life Insurance Company and Industrial Alliance Portfolio Management LLC are all part of iA Financial Group, one of the largest insurance and wealth management groups in North America. In the last few years, iA American has been thoughtfully built by iA Financial Group through the acquisition of several US based entities. Our suite of products and services includes automotive protection packages, reinsurance options, dealer support, direct-to-consumer products, in-house administration, life insurance, progressive special markets, and more!\\niA Financial Group is the fourth largest life and health insurance company in Canada and offers a wide range of products for all stages of life and to meet the needs of clients across its vast sales network. Founded in 1892, iA Financial Group’s stability and solidity make it an employer of choice that invests in its employees and their development over the long term. Our CEO Denis Ricard won #1 Insurance CEO in Canada from Glassdoor!\\nOur Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion \\nOur differences make us unique, and even stronger. That’s why, at iA Financial Group, we are committed to supporting and celebrating diversity. We are continually building a team that is as diverse as the people and communities we serve. By combining our different ways of seeing and experiencing the world, we will always be stronger than the sum of our parts! To learn more click here.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"iA American Warranty LP, American Amicable Group of Companies, iA American Life Insurance Company and Industrial Alliance Portfolio Management LLC are all part of iA Financial Group, one of the largest insurance and wealth management groups in North America.\",\"Founded in 1892, iA Financial Group’s stability and solidity make it an employer of choice that invests in its employees and their development over the long term.\",\"Our differences make us unique, and even stronger. That’s why, at iA Financial Group, we are committed to supporting and celebrating diversity.\",\"We are continually building a team that is as diverse as the people and communities we serve.\"],\"about_role\":\"As a Wash Bay Technician, you will play a key role in preparing vehicles for protective coatings and other shop services, ensuring high-quality results and excellent customer service. This position is a great opportunity to showcase your skills and fully realize your potential within a caring and trustworthy company that helps its clients feel confident and secure about their future.\",\"annual_salary\":[],\"benefits\":[\"Flexible Health, Dental and Vision insurance\",\"401(k) + company match\",\"PTO Plan\",\"Employee and family assistance program\",\"Ergonomic furniture program\",\"Performance bonus\"],\"education_level\":[],\"equal_opportunity\":[\"Great Lakes Companies and all its divisions are an Equal Opportunity Employer.\",\"We are committed to supporting and celebrating diversity.\",\"We are continually building a team that is as diverse as the people and communities we serve.\"],\"experience_level\":[\"Entry-level\"],\"location\":[\"Shop setting\"],\"requirements\":[\"Ability to learn new tasks and processes quickly and accurately\",\"Attention to detail and commitment to quality\",\"Strong work ethic in fast-paced environments\",\"Ability to follow procedures and maintain consistency\",\"Basic knowledge of vehicle washing and surface preparation\",\"Use hands to handle tools, reach, and communicate\",\"Stand, walk, stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl frequently\",\"Occasionally sit, climb, or balance\",\"Regularly lift/move up to 10 lbs., and occasionally up to 50 lbs.\",\"Maintain strong visual abilities (close, distance, color, peripheral, depth perception, focus)\",\"Stand and/or move most of the day with minimal sitting\",\"Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S.\",\"Unable to support or take over sponsorship of employment visas at this time, including H-1B visas and participation in STEM OPT work authorizations.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Prepare and wash vehicles for protective coating and related services\",\"Pay close attention to debris such as road tar and environmental particles\",\"Perform washing, claying, and surface preparation with precision\",\"Follow instructions, procedures, and processes to maintain service quality\",\"Provide great customer service while supporting overall shop operations\"],\"skills\":[\"Vehicle washing\",\"Surface preparation\"],\"work_type\":[\"Full-time\"]}},{\"id\":\"e88396b4-901c-4496-802f-3f8c695e0514\",\"source_id\":\"2406983948\",\"obfuscated_id\":41680908,\"title\":\"Software Support\",\"organization\":\"McCormick Systems\",\"job_url\":\"https://mccormicksystemsinc.isolvedhire.com/jobs/1852824\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-09T23:18:04.475494Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"AZ, US\",\"AZ, USA\",\"AZ, United States\",\"Arizona, US\",\"Arizona, USA\",\"Arizona, United States\",\"Chandler, AZ, US\",\"Chandler, AZ, USA\",\"Chandler, AZ, United States\",\"Chandler, Arizona, US\",\"Chandler, Arizona, USA\",\"Chandler, Arizona, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"c68fb015-f8ce-4d04-b986-a01986914e71\",\"company_image_id\":\"unlowhfbn98c5b5wo0tq\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"HOUR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":55000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":75000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Software support\",\"Technical troubleshooting\",\"Customer service\",\"Estimating software\",\"Communication skills\",\"Problem-solving\",\"Microsoft Outlook\",\"Microsoft Word\",\"Microsoft Excel\",\"CRM software\",\"Salesforce\",\"Documentation\",\"Construction industry knowledge\",\"Technical support\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"McCormick Systems\\nMcCormick Systems, a Foundation Software company, provides all-in-one takeoff and estimating software designed for the mechanical, electrical, and plumbing trades. For over 45 years, its solutions have helped estimators work more efficiently with features including patented Auto Home Run and Auto count functionality, trade-specific databases, and remote accessibility. \\nAs part of Foundation Software, McCormick Systems combines decades of industry expertise with innovative technology to help contractors simplify estimating and confidently pursue new opportunities.\\nPosition Summary\\nWe are seeking a knowledgeable and customer-oriented Software Support Representative to provide exceptional support for our suite of products. In this role, you will assist clients with technical issues, troubleshoot software problems, and ensure they are using the software efficiently to meet our customers' needs. Your expertise will help clients solve complex problems, offer guidance, and ensure a smooth user experience while also maintaining a high level of customer satisfaction.\\nEssential Functions and Responsibilities\\nProvide technical support to clients using estimating software, addressing issues via phone, email, or web.\\nTroubleshoot and resolve software-related problems, ensuring clients can efficiently process their daily tasks such as estimating, etc. and resolve discrepancies.\\nGuide clients through software updates, enhancements, and new features.\\nCollaborate with internal departments to resolve system issues, reporting issues, and to report any technical issues clients are experiencing.\\nMaintain expertise in the different software platforms, new modules, and any relevant industry changes.\\nEducate clients on best practices for using our products' features effectively.\\nTrack client issues using call-center software and ensure accurate and timely documentation of all support cases.\\nTrack and manage support tickets to ensure timely resolution and follow-up with clients as necessary.\\nAdhere to all department and company standard operating procedures and project a professional and positive image as a company representative.\\nStay up to date with changes in the industry, as well as software updates.\\nPerform other duties as assigned.\\nRequired Skills and Experience\\n1+ years of experience in software support\\nPayroll processing or estimating experience or involvement is a plus.\\nStrong understanding of estimating principles, and related software functionalities.\\nExperience working with customer service or technical support teams in a SaaS or software environment is preferred.\\nExcellent communication skills, both verbal and written, with the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical users in a clear and concise manner.\\nStrong problem-solving skills with the ability to troubleshoot complex issues independently while following established protocols.\\nProficient in using Microsoft Outlook, Word, and Excel; familiarity with Salesforce or other CRM software is a plus.\\nSuperior organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple support tickets simultaneously while prioritizing tasks effectively.\\nAbility to maintain detailed, accurate, and timely records.\\nBasic math skills.\\nKnowledge of the construction industry is a plus.\\nAbility to work well as part of a team and independently as needed.\\nMcCormick Systems is an Equal Opportunity Employer.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"McCormick Systems, a Foundation Software company, provides all-in-one takeoff and estimating software designed for the mechanical, electrical, and plumbing trades. For over 45 years, its solutions have helped estimators work more efficiently with features including patented Auto Home Run and Auto count functionality, trade-specific databases, and remote accessibility.\",\"As part of Foundation Software, McCormick Systems combines decades of industry expertise with innovative technology to help contractors simplify estimating and confidently pursue new opportunities.\"],\"about_role\":\"We are seeking a knowledgeable and customer-oriented Software Support Representative to provide exceptional support for our suite of products. In this role, you will assist clients with technical issues, troubleshoot software problems, and ensure they are using the software efficiently to meet our customers' needs. Your expertise will help clients solve complex problems, offer guidance, and ensure a smooth user experience while also maintaining a high level of customer satisfaction.\",\"annual_salary\":[],\"benefits\":[],\"education_level\":[],\"equal_opportunity\":[\"McCormick Systems is an Equal Opportunity Employer.\"],\"experience_level\":[\"1+ years of experience\"],\"location\":[],\"requirements\":[\"1+ years of experience in software support\",\"Payroll processing or estimating experience or involvement is a plus.\",\"Strong understanding of estimating principles, and related software functionalities.\",\"Experience working with customer service or technical support teams in a SaaS or software environment is preferred.\",\"Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written, with the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical users in a clear and concise manner.\",\"Strong problem-solving skills with the ability to troubleshoot complex issues independently while following established protocols.\",\"Proficient in using Microsoft Outlook, Word, and Excel; familiarity with Salesforce or other CRM software is a plus.\",\"Superior organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple support tickets simultaneously while prioritizing tasks effectively.\",\"Ability to maintain detailed, accurate, and timely records.\",\"Basic math skills.\",\"Knowledge of the construction industry is a plus.\",\"Ability to work well as part of a team and independently as needed.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Provide technical support to clients using estimating software, addressing issues via phone, email, or web.\",\"Troubleshoot and resolve software-related problems, ensuring clients can efficiently process their daily tasks such as estimating, etc. and resolve discrepancies.\",\"Guide clients through software updates, enhancements, and new features.\",\"Collaborate with internal departments to resolve system issues, reporting issues, and to report any technical issues clients are experiencing.\",\"Maintain expertise in the different software platforms, new modules, and any relevant industry changes.\",\"Educate clients on best practices for using our products' features effectively.\",\"Track client issues using call-center software and ensure accurate and timely documentation of all support cases.\",\"Track and manage support tickets to ensure timely resolution and follow-up with clients as necessary.\",\"Adhere to all department and company standard operating procedures and project a professional and positive image as a company representative.\",\"Stay up to date with changes in the industry, as well as software updates.\",\"Perform other duties as assigned.\"],\"skills\":[],\"work_type\":[]}},{\"id\":\"e78c6c9a-6f20-437f-a5c0-f411da87f87f\",\"source_id\":\"2380875507\",\"obfuscated_id\":40045316,\"title\":\"Software Tools Developer\",\"organization\":\"SOUTHEASTERN COMP CONSULTANTS INC\",\"job_url\":\"https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/4044E391B514AC0B5A7D9467CAC134FB/jobs/250024\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-09-24T20:20:28.233864Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Owens, VA, US\",\"Owens, VA, USA\",\"Owens, VA, United States\",\"Owens, Virginia, US\",\"Owens, Virginia, USA\",\"Owens, Virginia, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\",\"VA, US\",\"VA, USA\",\"VA, United States\",\"Virginia, US\",\"Virginia, USA\",\"Virginia, United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"bb5817c9-2dfb-4e7d-82c9-8fd79c24bb55\",\"company_image_id\":\"vtgp4zizjw3tn8wsry6w\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":95000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":135000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"C#\",\"C++\",\"VB.NET\",\"API Development And Integration\",\"SQL\",\"Software Development\",\"Configuration Management\",\"Hardware Configuration Management\",\"Database Tool Development\",\"Revision Control\",\"Baseline Management\",\"Change Control\",\"Release Management\",\"Power BI\",\"Power Automate\",\"Power Fx\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Job Details: Job Location: VA Potomac Drive Office - King George, VA, Salary Range: Undisclosed, Overview SCCI is seeking a Software Tools Developer to join our team! The successful candidate will be part of a team of Configuration Management (CM) Analysts working to manage CM information. This position ensures the integrity of the hardware baselines by managing and developing the critical Hardware CM database, drawing repositories, and change control pipelines that support our systems. This position is expected to interface with other functional areas (i.e. Hardware Engineering, CM, and JIRA IPT). This position is available for immediate hire and is located in Dahlgren, VA. SCCI offers a comprehensive and competitive benefits package including Health, Dental, Vision, Life and Disability benefits, 401k with Company Match, time off consisting of 2 weeks of paid vacation, 48 hours of sick/personal leave, and 11 paid Holidays. Responsibilities: Provide the BMS CM Lead with real-time visibility into the Hardware (HW) CM Database Tool. This includes reporting milestones, schedules, build status, and concerns Ensure that all Hardware CM Tool updates are conducted in accordance with Software and CM best practices Design, develop, test, and document the Hardware CM Tool progression to streamline CM drawing number assignment, revision control and system baselines. Collaborate weekly with the CM and JIRA teams Participate in continued BMS process improvements including but not limited to software development, configuration management, hardware engineering, and automation Be an active technical participant in the Database Tool Review Board (DTRB) is required Adapt to changing technologies, processes, and organizational requirements Providing timely and accurate information and status updates to leadership, project sponsors, end users, and management Providing timely alerts to the designated Government representative on potential issues Responsible for maintaining backlogs and providing work item estimations Participating in daily standup meetings : Essential Skills and Experience: Must be a U.S. Citizen and be able to obtain and maintain an active Secret Security Clearance High School Diploma Minimum of one (1) year of professional software development experience is required Demonstrated proficiency in C#, C++, and VB.net is required Direct experience developing and integrating Application Programming Interfaces (APIs) and writing Structured Query Language (SQL) functions is required Knowledge of Industry Best Practices for Software Development best practices is required Knowledge of Configuration Management processes and tools, including baseline identification, change control boards (CCB), configuration audits, release management, and status accounting is desired Ability to work in a fast paced, rapidly changing environment Ability to work independently and interface professionally with other government, contractor, and military organizations Ability to work with others to meet established goals and program schedules Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing Preferred Skills and Experience: CompTIA Security+ certification or desire to obtain one Experience with Power Suite tools and language (Power BI, Power Automate, and Power Fx) Experience training users and troubleshooting issues working with host site personnel and network engineers SCCI is committed to providing a comprehensive and competitive benefits package to meet the needs of employees and their families. EOE of Veterans and Disabilities.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"SCCI is committed to providing a comprehensive and competitive benefits package to meet the needs of employees and their families.\"],\"about_role\":\"SCCI is seeking a Software Tools Developer to manage CM information and ensure the integrity of hardware baselines by developing and managing the Hardware CM database, drawing repositories, and change control pipelines. This role involves interfacing with Hardware Engineering, CM, and JIRA IPT.\",\"annual_salary\":[\"Undisclosed\"],\"benefits\":[\"Health, Dental, Vision, Life and Disability benefits\",\"401k with Company Match\",\"2 weeks of paid vacation\",\"48 hours of sick/personal leave\",\"11 paid Holidays\"],\"education_level\":[\"High School Diploma\"],\"equal_opportunity\":[\"EOE of Veterans and Disabilities.\"],\"experience_level\":[\"1+ year professional software development experience\"],\"location\":[\"King George, VA\"],\"requirements\":[\"Must be a U.S. Citizen and able to obtain and maintain an active Secret Security Clearance.\",\"High School Diploma.\",\"Minimum of one (1) year of professional software development experience.\",\"Demonstrated proficiency in C#, C++, and VB.net.\",\"Direct experience developing and integrating Application Programming Interfaces (APIs) and writing Structured Query Language (SQL) functions.\",\"Knowledge of Industry Best Practices for Software Development.\",\"Knowledge of Configuration Management processes and tools, including baseline identification, change control boards (CCB), configuration audits, release management, and status accounting is desired.\",\"Ability to work in a fast-paced, rapidly changing environment.\",\"Ability to work independently and interface professionally with other government, contractor, and military organizations.\",\"Ability to work with others to meet established goals and program schedules.\",\"Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Provide the BMS CM Lead with real-time visibility into the Hardware (HW) CM Database Tool, including reporting milestones, schedules, build status, and concerns.\",\"Ensure all Hardware CM Tool updates are conducted in accordance with Software and CM best practices.\",\"Design, develop, test, and document the Hardware CM Tool progression to streamline CM drawing number assignment, revision control, and system baselines.\",\"Collaborate weekly with the CM and JIRA teams.\",\"Participate in continued BMS process improvements, including software development, configuration management, hardware engineering, and automation.\",\"Act as an active technical participant in the Database Tool Review Board (DTRB).\",\"Adapt to changing technologies, processes, and organizational requirements.\",\"Provide timely and accurate information and status updates to leadership, project sponsors, end users, and management.\",\"Provide timely alerts to the designated Government representative on potential issues.\",\"Maintain backlogs and provide work item estimations.\",\"Participate in daily standup meetings.\"],\"skills\":[\"C#\",\"C++\",\"VB.net\",\"API development and integration\",\"SQL\",\"Software Development Best Practices\",\"Configuration Management processes and tools\",\"Power Suite tools and language (Power BI, Power Automate, and Power Fx) (Preferred)\",\"User training and troubleshooting (Preferred)\"],\"work_type\":[\"Full-time\"]}},{\"id\":\"1472f133-a2db-4c7b-bdb9-0e2d4fd2476c\",\"source_id\":\"2418666449\",\"obfuscated_id\":42382249,\"title\":\"Software Application Developer\",\"organization\":\"ERPA\",\"job_url\":\"https://erpa.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ERPA/job/USA-TX-Remote/Software-Application-Developer_R1058\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-16T22:21:10.673383Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"TX, US\",\"TX, USA\",\"TX, United States\",\"Texas, US\",\"Texas, USA\",\"Texas, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":true,\"company_id\":\"d059fe9a-8cd1-8509-d8e8-5972275244c5\",\"company_image_id\":\"v1493198664/j9gg1v3rocmfck1i4rwt.png\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":85000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":130000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Software development\",\"Microservices\",\"Architecture design\",\"GIT\",\"Python\",\"Shell scripting\",\"PeopleSoft\",\"Workday\",\"Amazon Web Services\",\"System integration\",\"Unit testing\",\"Integration testing\",\"Technical documentation\",\"Requirement gathering\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"It's fun to work in a company where people truly BELIEVE in what they're doing!\\nWe're committed to bringing passion and customer focus to the business.\\nERPA is seeking a talented Software Application Developer.\\nExplore all our current Workday openings now: https://www.erpa.com/about-erpa/careers/\\nWhat We’re Offering\\nERPA Culture - Empathy | Responsibility | Passion | Agility\\nPaid time off plus paid holidays\\nMedical/dental/vision insurance plan\\nLife insurance, short/long term disability, and flex spending\\n401-k plan with a strong company match\\nWork From Home Opportunity\\nERPA is a leader in enterprise application managed services, cloud hosting, and consulting services. Our 500-plus consultants and technologists around the globe enable organizations to address their most complex challenges, including maximizing their technology investment and developing and executing future technology roadmaps for PeopleSoft, Workday, and Amazon Web Services.\\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\\nInvolve in architecting solutions for integrating with GIT plugins, PR builds, Release.\\nbuilds and internal deployment tools.\\nWork on architecture design decisions and discussions.\\nInvolve in Proof of Concepts \\u0026 technologies.\\nWork as product owner as well as this is completely technical implementation for the\\nWealth management, prepared requirements and also had written software requirements.\\nMicroservices development.\\nImplement modeling thoroughly based on the needs like performance of queries, storage,\\nPrepare and review high level design documents/low level design documents.\\nDesign / implementation / unit-integration testing for the project.\\nWrite shell / python scripting.\\nApplicants are considered for all positions in accordance with statutes and regulations concerning non-discrimination on the basis of race, ancestry, age, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, non-disqualifying disability, veteran status, or other protected classification. ERPA is an equal opportunity employer, as well as a substance and tobacco free workplace. All offers of employment are contingent on satisfactory pre-employment drug screen which may include reference checks, criminal background investigation, and when applicable licensing verification.\\nApplicants for this position in the United States must have work authorization that does not now or in the future require sponsorship of a visa for employment authorization in the United States and with ERPA.\\n\\nDISCLAIMER: Nothing in this job description restricts management's right to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities of this job.\\nReasonable Accommodations: ERPA provides reasonable accommodations to the known limitations of otherwise qualified employees and applicants for employment with disabilities, sincerely held religious beliefs, practices and observances, unless doing so would result in an undue hardship. Applicants for employment may request a reasonable accommodation/modification by contacting his/her recruiter.\\nNothing in this job description restricts management's right to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities of this job. \\nApplicants are considered for all positions in accordance with statutes and regulations concerning non-discrimination on the basis of race, ancestry, age, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, non-disqualifying disability, veteran status, or other protected classification.\\nERPA is an equal opportunity employer, as well as a substance and tobacco free workplace. All offers of employment are contingent on successfully passing the pre-employment drug screen and background investigation which may include reference checks, criminal background investigation, and when applicable licensing verification. \\nApplicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. We will not consider any applicants that require sponsorship for employment visa status either now or in the future.\\nIf you like wild growth and working with happy, enthusiastic over-achievers, you'll enjoy your career with us!\\nNotice: We use E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment eligibility of all new hires.\"},{\"id\":\"3394fd6c-e5a3-44b3-a89a-4c27a97cead3\",\"source_id\":\"2401638124\",\"obfuscated_id\":41286840,\"title\":\"Software Application Developer\",\"organization\":\"Torch Technologies, Inc.\",\"job_url\":\"https://starfish.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Eglin-AFB-FL/Software-Application-Developer_R1991\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-07T12:17:54.697352Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Eglin AFB, FL, US\",\"Eglin AFB, FL, USA\",\"Eglin AFB, FL, United States\",\"Eglin AFB, Florida, US\",\"Eglin AFB, Florida, USA\",\"Eglin AFB, Florida, United States\",\"FL, US\",\"FL, USA\",\"FL, United States\",\"Florida, US\",\"Florida, USA\",\"Florida, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"750d1ae9-aa46-4950-b3d6-2dd57fcebc1f\",\"company_image_id\":\"42452987a1aa4e95b839ec056156d8b0\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":85000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":120000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"C#\",\"VB.NET\",\"Python\",\"MATLAB\",\"SQL Server\",\"Electronic warfare\",\"Software development\",\"Relational databases\",\"SQL stored procedures\",\"Software development lifecycle\",\"Technical writing\",\"Machine learning\",\"Debugging\",\"Windows batch files\",\"Command-line automation\",\"Risk management framework\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Torch Technologies\\nThank you for your interest in employment with Torch Technologies. We are a 100% employee-owned, Certified Great Place To Work and named Best Places to Work in Huntsville/Madison County, headquartered in Huntsville, AL. Our team provides superior research, development, and engineering services to the Federal Government and Department of War. As one of the nation’s top 100 defense companies, the services we provide directly support the men and women who serve our country. Our corporate mission sums up the pride our employee-owners take in the work we do: “Lighting the Pathway of Freedom”. And, as a Certified Evergreen ESOP, we have made the commitment to grow and sustain our company for the next 100 years! Come grow with us!\\nTorch Technologies is seeking a Software Application Developer to join a team supporting the 16th Electronic Warfare Squadron (EWS), 350th Spectrum Warfare Wing (350 SWW), at Eglin AFB, Florida. The 350 SWW is the technical focal point for all electronic warfare (EW) support of warfighter systems for the Combat Air Forces (CAF). The mission of the 350 SWW is to develop and test mission data (MD) to defeat enemy radar and infrared guided missile systems, thus enhancing aircrew and aircraft survivability in combat. \\n\\nThis mission includes operational EW testing, MD development/validation/verification, force development evaluation execution and facilitating foreign materiel exploitation.\\n\\nAs a Software Application Developer, your duties will include the following, but are not limited to: \\n\\nSupport the production, test, and development environments by designing, developing, programming and maintaining Windows platform desktop and client/server applications in support of the 350th SWW. \\nTranslate technical issues and gather requirements/limitations from management and staff.\\nDevelop desktop and client/server applications with C#, VB.NET, Python, MATLAB, and SQL Server. \\nProvide advice and assistance with relational databases and interface applications to databases.\\nProvide advice and assistance with optimizing SQL stored procedures and functions. \\nAnalyze problems, design solutions, and optimize current/new techniques. \\nDeploy and maintain software and databases to customer sites and communicate with customers to diagnose and resolve technical customer issues. \\nProvide advice and assistance with understanding the software development lifecycle. \\nProvide advice and assistance with technical knowledge and writing requirements, design, and deployment documentations. \\nSupport an interest in Machine Learning to identify areas to modernize.\\n\\nRequired Qualifications: \\nU.S. Citizenship \\nA Bachelor’s or Master's degree in computer science, electrical engineering, or a related field, like math, science, or engineering.\\n3+ years experience with EW programs.\\n3-10 years experience software development.\\nStrong understanding of programming languages like C#, VB.NET, Python, MATLAB, and SQL Server\\nTechnical knowledge and good commenting background for code deployment documentation.\\nCommunication to interface with the customers in gathering requirements, diagnosing and resolving issues.\\nExperience coding, debugging and maintaining applications in aforementioned program languages\\nAnalyze problems at a fundamental level to design flexible solutions to optimize new techniques.\\nUnderstand software development lifecycle and knowledge of Risk Management Framework.\\nBe able to optimize SQL stored procedures/functions.\\nDetailed-oriented, focused, creative to tackle customer pain points in efficiency and generate scalable solutions.\\nFamiliar with Windows batch files and basic command-line automation.\\nPossess active Secret security clearance with the ability to obtain and maintain a Top Secret DoW Clearance. \\n\\nPreferred Qualifications:\\nA current active Top Secret or Secret security clearance is highly preferred.\\nDesired experience with machine learning for modernization efforts.\\nSchedule: M-F; 8-5\\nWork Location: Onsite, Eglin AFB, FL\\nRelocation Assistance Available: No\\nPosition Contingent Upon Award of Contract: No\\n\\n#LI-AP1\\n\\nBenefits: \\nTorch Technologies is proud to offer a stable and professional work environment, a competitive salary, and an excellent, comprehensive benefit package including: ESOP participation, 401(k) match, medical, dental, vision, life insurance, short-term disability, long-term disability, flexible spending accounts, Health Saving Accounts and Health Reimbursement Accounts, EAP, education assistance, paid time off, and holidays. \\nApplying to Torch Technologies: \\nOnly those candidates invited for an interview will be contacted. Employment at Torch Technologies is contingent upon the successful completion of a comprehensive background check. \\n­\\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, genetic information, citizenship, ancestry, marital status, protected veteran status, disability status or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law. Torch Technologies, Inc. participates in E-Verify. \\nIf you are a qualified individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, you have the right to request a reasonable accommodation if you are unable or limited in your ability to use or access Careers Link as a result of your disability. You can request reasonable accommodations by sending an email to HR@torchtechnologies.com. Thank you for your interest in Torch Technologies.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Torch Technologies is a 100% employee-owned, Certified Great Place To Work and named Best Places to Work in Huntsville/Madison County.\",\"Headquartered in Huntsville, AL, the company provides superior research, development, and engineering services to the Federal Government and Department of War.\",\"Torch Technologies is one of the nation’s top 100 defense companies.\",\"The corporate mission is “Lighting the Pathway of Freedom”.\",\"Torch Technologies is a Certified Evergreen ESOP, committed to growth for the next 100 years.\"],\"about_role\":\"Torch Technologies is seeking a Software Application Developer to support the 16th Electronic Warfare Squadron (EWS), 350th Spectrum Warfare Wing (350 SWW), at Eglin AFB, Florida. The 350 SWW is the technical focal point for all electronic warfare (EW) support of warfighter systems for the Combat Air Forces (CAF). The mission is to develop and test mission data (MD) to defeat enemy radar and infrared guided missile systems, thus enhancing aircrew and aircraft survivability in combat.\",\"annual_salary\":[],\"benefits\":[\"ESOP participation\",\"401(k) match\",\"Medical insurance\",\"Dental insurance\",\"Vision insurance\",\"Life insurance\",\"Short-term disability\",\"Long-term disability\",\"Flexible spending accounts\",\"Health Saving Accounts\",\"Health Reimbursement Accounts\",\"EAP\",\"Education assistance\",\"Paid time off\",\"Holidays\"],\"education_level\":[\"Bachelor's degree\",\"Master's degree\"],\"equal_opportunity\":[\"All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, genetic information, citizenship, ancestry, marital status, protected veteran status, disability status or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law.\",\"Torch Technologies, Inc. participates in E-Verify.\",\"If you are a qualified individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, you have the right to request a reasonable accommodation if you are unable or limited in your ability to use or access Careers Link as a result of your disability. You can request reasonable accommodations by sending an email to HR@torchtechnologies.com.\"],\"experience_level\":[\"3+ years experience with EW programs\",\"3-10 years experience software development\"],\"location\":[\"Eglin AFB, FL\"],\"requirements\":[\"U.S. Citizenship\",\"A Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in computer science, electrical engineering, or a related field, like math, science, or engineering.\",\"3+ years experience with EW programs.\",\"3-10 years experience software development.\",\"Strong understanding of programming languages like C#, VB.NET, Python, MATLAB, and SQL Server\",\"Technical knowledge and good commenting background for code deployment documentation.\",\"Communication to interface with the customers in gathering requirements, diagnosing and resolving issues.\",\"Experience coding, debugging and maintaining applications in aforementioned program languages\",\"Analyze problems at a fundamental level to design flexible solutions to optimize new techniques.\",\"Understand software development lifecycle and knowledge of Risk Management Framework.\",\"Be able to optimize SQL stored procedures/functions.\",\"Detailed-oriented, focused, creative to tackle customer pain points in efficiency and generate scalable solutions.\",\"Familiar with Windows batch files and basic command-line automation.\",\"Possess active Secret security clearance with the ability to obtain and maintain a Top Secret DoW Clearance.\",\"A current active Top Secret or Secret security clearance is highly preferred.\",\"Desired experience with machine learning for modernization efforts.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Support the production, test, and development environments by designing, developing, programming and maintaining Windows platform desktop and client/server applications in support of the 350th SWW.\",\"Translate technical issues and gather requirements/limitations from management and staff.\",\"Develop desktop and client/server applications with C#, VB.NET, Python, MATLAB, and SQL Server.\",\"Provide advice and assistance with relational databases and interface applications to databases.\",\"Provide advice and assistance with optimizing SQL stored procedures and functions.\",\"Analyze problems, design solutions, and optimize current/new techniques.\",\"Deploy and maintain software and databases to customer sites and communicate with customers to diagnose and resolve technical customer issues.\",\"Provide advice and assistance with understanding the software development lifecycle.\",\"Provide advice and assistance with technical knowledge and writing requirements, design, and deployment documentations.\",\"Support an interest in Machine Learning to identify areas to modernize.\"],\"skills\":[\"C#\",\"VB.NET\",\"Python\",\"MATLAB\",\"SQL Server\",\"Relational databases\",\"SQL stored procedures\",\"Software development lifecycle\",\"Risk Management Framework\",\"Windows batch files\",\"Command-line automation\",\"Machine Learning\"],\"work_type\":[\"Onsite\",\"Full-time\"]}},{\"id\":\"2539f82f-4bff-4ccc-846a-05a0ed6c549b\",\"source_id\":\"2395969111\",\"obfuscated_id\":40937669,\"title\":\"Software Intern\",\"organization\":\"Nordson Corporation\",\"job_url\":\"https://nordsonhcm.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/nordsoncareers/job/USA---Minnesota---Minneapolis---5900-Golden-Hills-Drive/Software-Intern_REQ52945\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-03T08:19:02.168194Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"MN, US\",\"MN, USA\",\"MN, United States\",\"Minneapolis, MN, US\",\"Minneapolis, MN, USA\",\"Minneapolis, MN, United States\",\"Minneapolis, Minnesota, US\",\"Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA\",\"Minneapolis, Minnesota, United States\",\"Minnesota, US\",\"Minnesota, USA\",\"Minnesota, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"0dcde547-e0a3-4a8a-b8a5-50999fdc9bd2\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":45000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":65000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"C#\",\"C++\",\"CUDA\",\"Azure Devops\",\"Visual Studio\",\"Matlab\",\"Python\",\"Winforms\",\"WPF\",\"Software development\",\"Unit testing\",\"Data analysis\",\"Problem-solving\",\"Communication\",\"Embedded systems\",\"User interface design\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Nordson is seeking a Software Engineering Intern to support new product development, continuous improvement, database migration, and devops projects at the Golden Valley site. This position will work closely with the Software Engineering, Firmware, Electrical, and Operations teams to develop new products, calibrate / certify products, maintain existing product lines, and continuously improve relevant code bases.\\nThe intern will gain hands-on experience in a fast-paced new product development and manufacturing environment and meaningfully contribute to projects that directly impact operational performance and business objectives.\\n\\nKey Responsibilities and Essential Functions:\\nParticipate in the new product development process.\\nWork with firmware engineers to communicate with embedded devices.\\nWork with systems engineers to calibrate and certify new and existing products.\\nWork with internal customers to resolve bugs on new and existing products.\\nWrite unit tests and stress tests for validation of software performance.\\nAssist in testing software releases for other members of the team.\\nAssists in collecting and processing data for our algorithm team.\\nParticipate in software process improvement team.\\nProvides recommendations for user interface improvements.\\nPerform additional software and engineering support activities as assigned.\\nCurrently pursuing a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related field.\\nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills.\\nAbility to organize and analyze data and communicate findings effectively.\\nStrong verbal and written communication skills.\\nSelf-motivated with the ability to manage multiple priorities.\\nAbility to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment.\\nFamiliarity with C#, c++/CLI, native c++, CUDA, Azure Devops, and / or Visual Studio is preferred.\\nExperience in Matlab or Python programming is preferred.\\nExperience with user interface design with Winforms and WPF is preferred.\\n\\nWhat You’ll Gain\\nReal world experience developing new products in a fast-paced environment while supporting existing products and production lines.Hands-on experience supporting software engineering operations in a global technology company.Exposure to production processes, manufacturing engineering practices, and operational improvement initiatives.Opportunity to lead and contribute to projects that deliver measurable business results.Mentorship from experienced Software Engineers.Experience collaborating with cross-functional teams across Operations, Electrical, Firmware, and Systems Engineering.Practical knowledge that supports academic studies and prepares you for a career in Software development.\\n\\nPhysical Demands:\\nThe physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this Job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee is frequently required to stand and sit.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Nordson is a global technology company.\"],\"about_role\":\"Nordson is seeking a Software Engineering Intern to support new product development, continuous improvement, database migration, and devops projects. This position will work closely with cross-functional teams to develop new products, calibrate/certify products, maintain existing product lines, and improve code bases. The intern will gain hands-on experience in a fast-paced development and manufacturing environment and contribute to projects impacting operational performance and business objectives.\",\"annual_salary\":[],\"benefits\":[\"Real world experience developing new products in a fast-paced environment while supporting existing products and production lines.\",\"Hands-on experience supporting software engineering operations in a global technology company.\",\"Exposure to production processes, manufacturing engineering practices, and operational improvement initiatives.\",\"Opportunity to lead and contribute to projects that deliver measurable business results.\",\"Mentorship from experienced Software Engineers.\",\"Experience collaborating with cross-functional teams across Operations, Electrical, Firmware, and Systems Engineering.\",\"Practical knowledge that supports academic studies and prepares you for a career in Software development.\"],\"education_level\":[\"Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related field\"],\"equal_opportunity\":[],\"experience_level\":[\"Intern\"],\"location\":[\"Golden Valley\"],\"requirements\":[\"Currently pursuing a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related field.\",\"Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\",\"Ability to organize and analyze data and communicate findings effectively.\",\"Strong verbal and written communication skills.\",\"Self-motivated with the ability to manage multiple priorities.\",\"Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Participate in the new product development process.\",\"Work with firmware engineers to communicate with embedded devices.\",\"Work with systems engineers to calibrate and certify new and existing products.\",\"Work with internal customers to resolve bugs on new and existing products.\",\"Write unit tests and stress tests for validation of software performance.\",\"Assist in testing software releases for other members of the team.\",\"Assist in collecting and processing data for the algorithm team.\",\"Participate in software process improvement team.\",\"Provide recommendations for user interface improvements.\",\"Perform additional software and engineering support activities as assigned.\"],\"skills\":[\"C#\",\"C++/CLI\",\"Native C++\",\"CUDA\",\"Azure DevOps\",\"Visual Studio\",\"Matlab\",\"Python\",\"Winforms\",\"WPF\"],\"work_type\":[\"Internship\"]}},{\"id\":\"e1f0648f-4265-4834-b306-a181d923dfd3\",\"source_id\":\"2390109553\",\"obfuscated_id\":40581615,\"title\":\"Software Application Developer\",\"organization\":\"Jedson Engineering Inc\",\"job_url\":\"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c77dff2c-a031-4a23-9e4b-bef16b74328c\\u0026jobId=25297\\u0026ccId=19000101_000003\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-09-30T17:22:41.0898Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Cincinnati, OH, US\",\"Cincinnati, OH, USA\",\"Cincinnati, OH, United States\",\"Cincinnati, Ohio, US\",\"Cincinnati, Ohio, USA\",\"Cincinnati, Ohio, United States\",\"OH, US\",\"OH, USA\",\"OH, United States\",\"Ohio, US\",\"Ohio, USA\",\"Ohio, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"2c62f877-01f6-4378-adfd-16852e050ee1\",\"company_image_id\":\"v1509759683/fpiarrtguz7itdlfmt88.svg\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":75000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":110000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"PHP\",\"JavaScript\",\"Webix\",\"Microsoft SQL Server\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"SQL\",\"API Integrations\",\"IIS\",\"Git\",\"Web Services\",\"Application Development\",\"Database Management\",\"Reporting\",\"Troubleshooting\",\"Requirements Gathering\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\" \\n\\nSoftware Developer \\n\\n\\n\\n\\nWill need to work in the Jedson Cin, OH office. Hybrid Schedule \\n\\n\\n\\n\\nPosition Summary\\n\\nJedson Engineering is seeking an Application Developer to support, enhance, and modernize our internally developed business platform.\\n\\nThis role will develop and maintain business-critical applications used across project operations, reporting, finance, project controls, and engineering processes. The successful candidate will work closely with business stakeholders, developers, and our DBA/SQL Engineer to deliver application enhancements, integrations, reporting solutions, and process improvements.\\n\\nThe ideal candidate has hands-on experience with PHP, JavaScript, Webix, and Microsoft SQL Server and enjoys solving business problems through technology.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nResponsibilities\\n\\n * Develop, maintain, and support the Insight platform and related business applications.\\n * Build and enhance web-based user interfaces using JavaScript, Webix, HTML, and CSS.\\n * Develop and maintain backend application functionality using PHP.\\n * Create, modify, and optimize SQL queries, views, reports, and stored procedures.\\n * Collaborate with business stakeholders to gather requirements and implement solutions.\\n * Develop and maintain integrations with internal and third-party systems using APIs and web services.\\n * Troubleshoot and resolve application, database, reporting, and integration issues.\\n * Participate in testing, deployments, documentation, and ongoing application support.\\n * Identify opportunities to automate processes and improve operational efficiency.\\n * Contribute to future application modernization initiatives and new application development efforts.\\n\\nRequired Qualifications\\n\\n * Professional experience developing applications using PHP.\\n * Professional experience developing web applications using JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.\\n * Experience working with Webix or similar JavaScript UI frameworks.\\n * Experience writing and troubleshooting SQL queries against relational databases.\\n * Experience working with Microsoft SQL Server.\\n * Experience developing or supporting API integrations.\\n * Familiarity with IIS and Windows-hosted web applications.\\n * Strong analytical, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills.\\n * Strong written and verbal communication skills.\\n * Ability to work directly with business users to understand requirements and deliver solutions.\\n * Experience using source control systems such as Git.\\n\\nPreferred Qualifications\\n\\n * Experience supporting internally developed line-of-business applications.\\n * Exposure to C#, ASP.NET, or .NET development.\\n * Experience with Deltek Vision or Deltek Vantagepoint.\\n * Experience in the engineering, architecture, construction, or professional services industry.\\n * Experience with reporting, ERP, project management, or operational business systems.\\n * Experience working with enterprise software integrations and data synchronization processes.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Jedson Engineering is seeking an Application Developer to support, enhance, and modernize our internally developed business platform.\"],\"about_role\":\"Jedson Engineering is seeking an Application Developer to support, enhance, and modernize our internally developed business platform. This role will develop and maintain business-critical applications used across project operations, reporting, finance, project controls, and engineering processes. The successful candidate will work closely with business stakeholders, developers, and our DBA/SQL Engineer to deliver application enhancements, integrations, reporting solutions, and process improvements.\",\"annual_salary\":[],\"benefits\":[],\"education_level\":[],\"equal_opportunity\":[],\"experience_level\":[],\"location\":[\"Jedson Cin, OH\"],\"requirements\":[\"Professional experience developing applications using PHP.\",\"Professional experience developing web applications using JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.\",\"Experience working with Webix or similar JavaScript UI frameworks.\",\"Experience writing and troubleshooting SQL queries against relational databases.\",\"Experience working with Microsoft SQL Server.\",\"Experience developing or supporting API integrations.\",\"Familiarity with IIS and Windows-hosted web applications.\",\"Strong analytical, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills.\",\"Strong written and verbal communication skills.\",\"Ability to work directly with business users to understand requirements and deliver solutions.\",\"Experience using source control systems such as Git.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Develop, maintain, and support the Insight platform and related business applications.\",\"Build and enhance web-based user interfaces using JavaScript, Webix, HTML, and CSS.\",\"Develop and maintain backend application functionality using PHP.\",\"Create, modify, and optimize SQL queries, views, reports, and stored procedures.\",\"Collaborate with business stakeholders to gather requirements and implement solutions.\",\"Develop and maintain integrations with internal and third-party systems using APIs and web services.\",\"Troubleshoot and resolve application, database, reporting, and integration issues.\",\"Participate in testing, deployments, documentation, and ongoing application support.\",\"Identify opportunities to automate processes and improve operational efficiency.\",\"Contribute to future application modernization initiatives and new application development efforts.\"],\"skills\":[\"PHP\",\"JavaScript\",\"Webix\",\"Microsoft SQL Server\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"SQL\",\"API integrations\",\"IIS\",\"Git\"],\"work_type\":[\"Hybrid Schedule\"]}},{\"id\":\"e8ecc5a0-a88c-4bfe-adb4-7b42e59585d8\",\"source_id\":\"2379320817\",\"obfuscated_id\":39965241,\"title\":\"Software Intern\",\"organization\":\"HPE\",\"job_url\":\"https://careers.hpe.com/us/en/job/1215275/Software-Intern\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-09-24T02:19:01.489391Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Aguadilla, PR\",\"Aguadilla, PRI\",\"Aguadilla, Puerto Rico\",\"PR\",\"PRI\",\"Puerto Rico\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"7119654e-66d3-6617-13a8-09f99abdb9fa\",\"company_image_id\":\"xqkg9ih5mdbodkxnckvh\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":30000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":45000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Software systems design\",\"Programming\",\"Debugging\",\"Analytical skills\",\"Problem-solving\",\"Communication skills\",\"Testing procedures\",\"Coding\",\"Operating systems\",\"Compilers\",\"Networking\",\"Databases\",\"Internet-related tools\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Software Intern\\nThis role has been designed as 'Hybrid' with a requirement that you will work on average 2 days per week from an HPE office.\\nWho We Are:\\nHewlett Packard Enterprise is the global edge-to-cloud company advancing the way people live and work. We help companies connect, protect, analyze, and act on their data and applications wherever they live, from edge to cloud, so they can turn insights into outcomes at the speed required to thrive in today’s complex world. Our culture thrives on finding new and better ways to accelerate what’s next. We know varied backgrounds are valued and succeed here. We have the flexibility to manage our work and personal needs. We make bold moves, together, and are a force for good. If you are looking to stretch and grow your career our culture will embrace you. Open up opportunities with HPE.\\nJob Description:\\nJob Description:\\nThis requisition may be classified as on desk or hybrid depending on location and role.\\n\\nJob Family Definition:\\nDesigns, develops, troubleshoots and debugs software programs for software enhancements and new products. Develops software including operating systems, compilers, routers, networks, utilities, databases and Internet-related tools. Determines hardware compatibility and/or influences hardware design.\\n\\nManagement Level Definition:\\nContributes to assignments of limited scope by applying technical concepts and theoretical knowledge acquired through specialized training, education, or previous experience. Acts as team member by providing information, analysis and recommendations in support of team efforts. Exercises independent judgment within defined parameters.\\n\\nResponsibilities:\\n• Codes and programs enhancements, updates, and changes for portions and subsystems of systems software, including operating systems, compliers, networking, utilities, databases, and Internet-related tools\\n• Executes established test plans and protocols for assigned portions of code; identifies, logs, and debugs assigned issues.\\n• Develops understanding of and relationship with internal and outsourced development partners on software systems design and development.\\n• Participates as a member of a project team of other software systems engineers and internal and outsourced development partners to develop reliable, cost effective and high quality solutions for low to moderately- complex products.\\n\\nIntern Education \\u0026 Experience Required:\\nWorking towards a Bachelor's and/or Master's degree with a focus in Computer Science, Information Systems, or equivalent.\\n\\nKnowledge and Skills:\\n• Experience or understanding of software systems design tools and languages.\\n• Good analytical and problem-solving skills.\\n• Understanding of design for software systems running on multiple platform types\\n• Good written and verbal communication skills; mastery in English and local language.\\n• Understanding of basic testing, coding, and debugging procedures\\n• Good written and verbal communication skills; mastery in English and local language.\\n\\n\\nAccessibility\\n\\nHPE is committed to creating an inclusive and accessible workplace and encourages applications from all qualified individuals, including those with disabilities. If you believe you require accommodation during any stage of the application or interview process, please submit your request by completing our secure form linked here.\\n\\nNote: This option is reserved for applicants needing assistance/reasonable accommodation related to a disability.\\nWhat We Can Offer You:\\nHealth \\u0026 Wellbeing\\nWe strive to provide our team members and their loved ones with a comprehensive suite of benefits that supports their physical, financial and emotional wellbeing.\\nPersonal \\u0026 Professional Development\\nWe also invest in your career because the better you are, the better we all are. We have specific programs catered to helping you reach any career goals you have — whether you want to become a knowledge expert in your field or apply your skills to another division.\\nUnconditional Inclusion\\nWe are unconditionally inclusive in the way we work and celebrate individual uniqueness. We know varied backgrounds are valued and succeed here. We have the flexibility to manage our work and personal needs. We make bold moves, together, and are a force for good.\\nLet's Stay Connected:\\nFollow @HPECareers on Instagram to see the latest on people, culture and tech at HPE. \\nJob:\\nEngineering\\nJob Level:\\nN/A\\nHPE is an Equal Employment Opportunity/ Veterans/Disabled/LGBT employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, or any other protected category, and all decisions we make are made on the basis of qualifications, merit, and business need. Our goal is to be one global team that is representative of our customers, in an inclusive environment where we can continue to innovate and grow together. Please click here: Equal Employment Opportunity.\\nHewlett Packard Enterprise is EEO Protected Veteran/ Individual with Disabilities.\\nHPE will comply with all applicable laws related to employer use of arrest and conviction records, including laws requiring employers to consider for employment qualified applicants with criminal histories.\\nRecruitment Fraud Alert\\nWe have become aware of an increase in fraudulent recruitment activities in which individuals impersonate our company or authorized recruitment agencies to offer fake employment opportunities. These scams may occur through false websites, emails, social media, or chat-based applications and often aim to obtain personal information or money. Please note that Hewlett Packard Enterprise (HPE), its direct and indirect subsidiaries and affiliated companies, and its authorized recruitment agencies/vendors will never charge a candidate a registration fee, hiring fee, or any other fee in connection with its recruitment and hiring process. We also never request personal information such as back account details, Social Security numbers, or national IDs via social media or chat applications.\\nAll legitimate job opportunities will come through official company channels, and candidates are responsible for verifying the credentials of any third party claiming to represent the company. Any reliance on fraudulent communication is at the individual’s own risk, and HPE disclaims legal liability for any resulting damages. If you suspect recruitment fraud, do not share personal information or make any payments and report the incident to your local authorities immediately.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Hewlett Packard Enterprise is the global edge-to-cloud company advancing the way people live and work.\",\"We help companies connect, protect, analyze, and act on their data and applications wherever they live, from edge to cloud, so they can turn insights into outcomes at the speed required to thrive in today’s complex world.\",\"Our culture thrives on finding new and better ways to accelerate what’s next.\",\"We know varied backgrounds are valued and succeed here.\",\"We have the flexibility to manage our work and personal needs.\",\"We make bold moves, together, and are a force for good.\",\"If you are looking to stretch and grow your career our culture will embrace you.\",\"Open up opportunities with HPE.\"],\"about_role\":\"Designs, develops, troubleshoots, and debugs software programs for software enhancements and new products. Develops software including operating systems, compilers, routers, networks, utilities, databases, and Internet-related tools. Determines hardware compatibility and/or influences hardware design.\",\"annual_salary\":[],\"benefits\":[\"Health \\u0026 Wellbeing\",\"Personal \\u0026 Professional Development\",\"Unconditional Inclusion\"],\"education_level\":[\"Bachelor's degree\",\"Master's degree\"],\"equal_opportunity\":[\"HPE is an Equal Employment Opportunity/ Veterans/ Disabled/ LGBT employer.\",\"We do not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, or any other protected category, and all decisions we make are made on the basis of qualifications, merit, and business need.\",\"Our goal is to be one global team that is representative of our customers, in an inclusive environment where we can continue to innovate and grow together.\",\"Hewlett Packard Enterprise is EEO Protected Veteran/ Individual with Disabilities.\",\"HPE will comply with all applicable laws related to employer use of arrest and conviction records, including laws requiring employers to consider for employment qualified applicants with criminal histories.\"],\"experience_level\":[\"Intern\"],\"location\":[\"Hybrid\"],\"requirements\":[\"Working towards a Bachelor's and/or Master's degree with a focus in Computer Science, Information Systems, or equivalent.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Codes and programs enhancements, updates, and changes for portions and subsystems of systems software, including operating systems, compilers, networking, utilities, databases, and Internet-related tools.\",\"Executes established test plans and protocols for assigned portions of code; identifies, logs, and debugs assigned issues.\",\"Develops understanding of and relationship with internal and outsourced development partners on software systems design and development.\",\"Participates as a member of a project team of other software systems engineers and internal and outsourced development partners to develop reliable, cost effective and high quality solutions for low to moderately- complex products.\"],\"skills\":[\"Experience or understanding of software systems design tools and languages.\",\"Good analytical and problem-solving skills.\",\"Understanding of design for software systems running on multiple platform types.\",\"Good written and verbal communication skills; mastery in English and local language.\",\"Understanding of basic testing, coding, and debugging procedures.\"],\"work_type\":[\"Hybrid\"]}},{\"id\":\"77f3eae6-a3bd-4081-b2dc-e43505702a36\",\"source_id\":\"2379013651\",\"obfuscated_id\":39949417,\"title\":\"Software Intern\",\"organization\":\"Hewlett Packard Enterprise\",\"job_url\":\"https://hpe.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WFMathpe/job/Aguadilla-Puerto-Rico-Puerto-Rico/Software-Intern_1215275\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-09-23T23:19:32.974441Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Aguadilla, PR\",\"Aguadilla, PRI\",\"Aguadilla, Puerto Rico\",\"PR\",\"PRI\",\"Puerto Rico\",\"San Juan, PR\",\"San Juan, PRI\",\"San Juan, Pue